            <ArticleTitle>Giant hepatocellular adenoma in a previously obese thirteen-year-old boy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>559-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hepatocellular adenoma is an uncommon neoplasm, especially in the childhood age group. We describe a previously obese 13-year-old male with a giant hepatocellular adenoma requiring an extensive hepatic resection. The related pediatric tumor literature, diagnosis and clinical management is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
